nding over $2M on TV, keeping the race competitive"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point to a clear but not overwhelming Lee advantage: incumbency, a modestly Democratic-leaning district, and a consensus of Likely D ratings, with markets pricing her near 94%. O'Donnell's substantial fundraising and the district's history of close margins argue for a somewhat narrower expected margin than the safest ratings imply.", "watch": "A late polling shift toward O'Donnell or heavy outside spending in the final week could pull this into Lean D territory.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Susie Lee (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Nevada's 3rd District pairs a well-funded incumbent, Susie Lee, against Trump-backed Republican Marty O'Donnell, who has raised nearly $5 million and committed to more than $2 million in television spending. The district leans only slightly Democratic, and its last two elections were decided by fewer than four points, so the underlying electorate is genuinely competitive.\n\nStill, the evidence favors Lee. Most expert raters place the race at Likely D or better, a late October poll showed her up seven, and prediction markets price her chances around 94%. With her cash advantage and incumbency, she enters the final stretch as a clear but not certain favorite.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9366, "margin": 9.91}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9036, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9329, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9282, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9091, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.906, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9242, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.942, "margin": 10.2}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.921, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9325, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.93, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9287, "margin": 9.5}, {"date"